From 7f33e9fbf83059a0a1ed5e530f463124ce1e4be0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@soprasteria.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 18:17:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: measure the arc angle at each blast grid, not the
 target

The arc delineation test reoriented the spell's target grid instead of
the grid the blast scan was looking at, so every grid received the same
angle difference: an arc counted every monster in range and line of
sight, or none.  In practice the constant passed, and arcs were rated
as full balls.  Use the scanned grid (ry, rx) for the table lookup.

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-fight-attack.c b/src/borg/borg-fight-attack.c
index 45c5d140a..f898a9a1a 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-fight-attack.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-fight-attack.c
@@ -1966,8 +1966,8 @@ static int borg_launch_arc_at_location(
 
             /* check on angle */
             /* Reorient current grid for table access. */
-            n2y = y - y1 + 20;
-            n2x = x - x1 + 20;
+            n2y = ry - y1 + 20;
+            n2x = rx - x1 + 20;
 
             /* Find the angular difference (/2) between the lines to
                 * the end of the arc's center-line and to the current grid.
